 a mix  but yeah look it's it's uh it's a  difficult  uh choice to make it's you know  sometimes financial sometimes it's  creative um but you know i think it's  hard just to hold on and kind of oh what  about sundance oh what about this um  you know you just don't know  yeah and by the way i've spoken to so  many people there is no right answer  because i've i've also spoken to people  who have made really good movies and  they're totally expecting to sell at the  festival and then it's sort of quiet and  then you know like i i think just  congratulations on selling your movie  and getting it out  that's the most important thing i was  just curious how it go how you guys  discussed it you know um kristen so the  movie's called alice obviously how many  other alt titles did you have or is it  always alice uh the first title was 55  acres and then peter i think it was you  or someone told me  oh that sounds like spike lee's  production company  so so i changed the name and then i i  was  thinking of what should i call it and i  was like duh call it alice  because it's about alice and she  she is she's the entire story  um kiki you have  a number of very powerful moments in the  film and i'm just curious  you have a i was gonna curse a very  large scene  on like a monday and um and you know  you're going to have to emotionally  deliver how early on are you preparing  for that moment in your head with the  dialogue and how you want to play  how it is for me  it's living and building up for me  before i even set foot on stage and i  don't know how healthy that is but  that that's how i've been doing it since  i was a kid that it literally starts to  live in me and the concept and the  feelings and the emotions of the  character start to become a part of my  everyday life from the moment that i say  i'm doing this role it literally you  know i could be eating food or something  like how would alice eat food it would  just come to me you know what i mean  just because i k