n she could have  was through the stories that her her  mother or father or any of the relatives  had  and um it was not only  how she  handled herself growing up that way but  when she  did run away  how she  empowered herself and what she did with  her life and the the biggest difference  between  all of those stories and alice is  the  all of them took place in the 60s and i  wanted alice to emerge into the 70s when  there's been a little bit of time to  reflect on the civil rights movement and  have a character like frank that was a  part of that movement and has lost  hope because he's like man it didn't go  anywhere and for her to be that spark  for him  and um so yeah that was the the  biggest thing was the 70s but everything  else  sadly the the stories that i read were  were  so so um  violent  uh that i i wouldn't put that in the  movie but  yeah  for all three of you um i love learning  about like the random behind-the-scenes  stories fun stuff about the making of  the film even though this is a very  powerful movie um so for all three of  you what do you think might surprise  people to learn about the actual making  of the film  you know maybe i mean i don't know if  they would be surprised by this but we  really were having a good time with one  another i mean yes there was some heavy  stuff and those scenes were difficult  but  i have nothing but fond memories of  shooting atlas you know uh you know i  really loved working with christian i  loved working with peter i loved being  in savannah i loved working with common  um all of us couldn't wait to get to the  70s portion of the movie needless to say  but you know it was a it was an  enjoyable time it was we were bonding  and you know it all was happening  interestingly enough around the around  the election as well  um so it was just a lot of energy and  it was it was a it was a wonderful time  filming that movie  and cove had brought us closer because  we all were in alignment of if one of us  messe