n you have a character  like alice it's like man who will really  like give her an injection of like no  this is like i'm gonna take matters into  my own hands like of course pampers that  person and of course coffee is that  movie i i know we have to wrap up but do  you have any sort of personal connection  to pam what does she mean to you  um in in regards to  her representation and how the community  feels about her my mom has always you  know so crazy but my mom always said  you're like pam greer she would always  mention pam greer in my life you know  about representation and how she feels  about me and my power and how i can own  my power as an entertainer as a talent  you know my mom has always said you know  you know um encouraging things like that  to me um but i think i really did my  real research on the artwork uh of pam  grier with kristen you know coming into  alice that was a big part of  the movie for her and for me to really  dive into so it went from hearing how  people feel about pam grier  understanding what she means and kind of  just feeling like i know her because of  that and then doing my own personal  research i just think she was such a  strong you know black woman at the time  it was you know i think very very  outspoken in a in a great way in already  a tough industry and i think you know  she almost had kind of this superhero uh  nature about her which i think you know  kiki and alice kind of uh embodies in  that kind of you know second half of the  movie  in life  that answer change i would say kiki  palmer is my hero  and i'm not just saying that like it's  she's all our hero  on that note i really want to say a  sincere congratulation uh  congratulations on this film uh i know  people are going to enjoy this one and  uh congrats on being part of the  sundance film festival and i really  appreciate you guys talking to me about  the movie i wish you all nothing but the  best and good luck with the rest of your  speed dating  you
 

